// codebox_enc.gen -- f_vf_lbm: upsample the 192x108 velocity to the render size, apply gain, clamp, encode as an
// f_vecfield (RG = XY, 0.5 = zero, B = 0.5, A = 1) and apply the bypass gate. Runs at RENDER resolution.
// Mirror: tests/modules/vf_lbm/vf_lbm_mirror.encode() (at the solver size this is exactly that function).
//
// Inlets: first = `r draw` bang (unused; it triggers every frame and gives this pix the render-context size),
// second = the macro texture (R = ux, G = uy) from the mac stage, third = the previous step's macro texture
// from the mprev stage.
//   - SPEED BLEND: the velocity shown is mix(previous, current, phase / nsteps). The frame gate sends phase = 1..N
//     (the frame within the current solver step) and nsteps = N, so at Speed 1/N the output moves smoothly
//     between solver steps (about N frames behind). Defaults phase 1, nsteps 1: the current velocity only.
//   - FR-008: R = clamp(0.5 + gain * ux, 0, 1), G likewise with uy. The velocity is in lattice units
//     (inflow up to 0.1), so the default gain of 3 puts the free stream near 0.74 and keeps the faster flow
//     around the obstacle inside the range (gain 1 would sit within 0.05 of the centre).
//   - the upsample is a manual 4-tap bilinear on texel-centre nearest() taps: y periodic (the solver's y is
//     periodic), x clamped to the end columns (the channel is not periodic in x). An edge feather (outer 3
//     columns copied from the inner neighbour) was tried 2026-10-21 and REMOVED the same day: it smeared the
//     noisy inner column into horizontal streak bands and did not contain the jitter, which reaches 7+ columns in
//     from the left edge while Wind is swept down.
//   - a non-finite sample encodes as zero velocity (abs(x) < 1e30 guard), so no NaN or Inf reaches the outlet
//   - bypass_gate = 1 outputs an exactly neutral field (zero velocity). The solver keeps running upstream.
//     The Param is never named `bypass` (native pix attribute).
vxm(u, v, w) {
  return mix(nearest(in3, vec(u, v)).x, nearest(in2, vec(u, v)).x, w);
}
vym(u, v, w) {
  return mix(nearest(in3, vec(u, v)).y, nearest(in2, vec(u, v)).y, w);
}

Param gain(3);
Param bypass_gate(0);
Param phase(1);
Param nsteps(1);

W = 192;
H = 108;
bw = clamp(phase / max(nsteps, 1), 0, 1);
fx = norm.x * W - 0.5;
fy = norm.y * H - 0.5;
x0 = floor(fx);
y0 = floor(fy);
tx = fx - x0;
ty = fy - y0;
xa = (min(max(x0, 0), W - 1) + 0.5) / W;
xb = (min(max(x0 + 1, 0), W - 1) + 0.5) / W;
ya = (wrap(y0, 0, H) + 0.5) / H;
yb = (wrap(y0 + 1, 0, H) + 0.5) / H;
au = mix(mix(vxm(xa, ya, bw), vxm(xb, ya, bw), tx), mix(vxm(xa, yb, bw), vxm(xb, yb, bw), tx), ty);
av = mix(mix(vym(xa, ya, bw), vym(xb, ya, bw), tx), mix(vym(xa, yb, bw), vym(xb, yb, bw), tx), ty);
au = switch(abs(au) < 1e30, au, 0);
av = switch(abs(av) < 1e30, av, 0);

r = clamp(0.5 + gain * au, 0, 1);
g = clamp(0.5 + gain * av, 0, 1);
out1 = vec(mix(r, 0.5, bypass_gate), mix(g, 0.5, bypass_gate), 0.5, 1);
